GOAL - Learn Pygame efficently to improve the ui in the new stock sim

Learnt basic pygame using a porject based youtube tutorial, now try to build frozen hunt game project.

1. imported basic PyGame starting frame from their offical website
2. set fps = 60, screen size = 1280 x 720.
3. Character Class - created a caharcter class that lets the inputted image get cut up into the specifc frames i need for both the animation and movement (gets the first 3 rows of images (white sprite)). The sprite starts with direction facing forwards(self.all_frames[4]) and the position will be the centre of the screen. A dictionary called direction index is created to find out what animation frame is called when the character moves a certain direction. In the update method, change in x(dx) and change in y(dy) is calculated based on player input and if it isnt (0,0) then the image of the charcter changes based on the direction and animation speed. The player position is then updated to calculate offset and the rectangle's center always satys at the centre pof the screen.
4. camera offset is calculated to be added to later objcets/sprites
5. basic frozen mechanic is added to the game ,with different timers that are created to calculate time frozen(2s) and time unfrozen(5s), depending if its frozen or unfrozen the background will chnage to either grey or blue.
6. Enemy/spider sprite - Outside of the sprite class, created a 2D array list to hold the correct frame for animations, cuts through each row (8) and for each column of 12 it cuts out each indiviudal sprite and puts in inside the frames list, then that list is placed into the total frames list. Inside the enemy/spider class, different attributes where given, like the image,rect,pos,etc. Then inside the update method, distance between the player and the spider is calculated so the spider can follow in the direction of the player. dx,dy is the found so the correct index for the frames list can be found in the direction_index list. Then the animation is done (same method as the character class). However, this time when displaying the spider offset needs to be subtracted so the spider is on the screen.
7. Creating an infinite background. Blue and Normal backgorund were both imported, inside the game_active loop varibles were created to find the start x/y of the offsetted screen, it is then looped so the background can be duplicated and placed into the screen where it changes depending on the offset.
8. Start screen. Created a pixel type font and made the text say "FROZEN HUNT" and created a rect so its not affected by the offset. It is then blit on screen along with the character sprite image 4 (facing down) not affected by offset too. Then a backgorund is needed where it was just looped between -1 and 3 to create a full background so that it doesnt look streched.
